      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.66,
          "end": 4.2,
          "en": "So what are pipes?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.2,
          "end": 6.96,
          "en": "Well, in the end, in Angular,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.96,
          "end": 10.92,
          "en": "pipes are a thing you can add in your templates",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.92,
          "end": 15.92,
          "en": "to transform the way data is displayed on the screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 16.26,
          "end": 20.67,
          "en": "to transform values or how values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 20.67,
          "end": 23.01,
          "en": "are formatted and displayed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 23.01,
          "end": 25.89,
          "en": "when being used in your templates.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.89,
          "end": 30.33,
          "en": "And we saw an example for a built-in pipe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 30.33,
          "end": 32.49,
          "en": "being used earlier in the course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.49,
          "end": 36.45,
          "en": "with the currency pipe that could be used in a template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 36.45,
          "end": 41.37,
          "en": "to make sure that value is output formatted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 41.37,
          "end": 45.75,
          "en": "as a currency with the currency's symbol",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 45.75,
          "end": 49.32,
          "en": "and by also formatting the number in a certain way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 49.32,
          "end": 53.7,
          "en": "And there we did use such an Angular pipe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 53.7,
          "end": 57.21,
          "en": "Now Angular does actually not just chip",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 57.21,
          "end": 59.13,
          "en": "with the currency pipe,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 59.13,
          "end": 61.92,
          "en": "but with a couple of other pipes as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 61.92,
          "end": 64.17,
          "en": "And we'll see some of these pipes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 64.17,
          "end": 66.27,
          "en": "in action throughout this course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 66.27,
          "end": 68.55,
          "en": "and of course also in this section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 68.55,
          "end": 72.03,
          "en": "And we'll also explore how we can use these pipes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 72.03,
          "end": 74.97,
          "en": "and configure them in our templates.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 74.97,
          "end": 79.47,
          "en": "And therefore, attached, you find another Angular project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 79.47,
          "end": 82.68,
          "en": "which you can download and extract and run NPM install.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 82.68,
          "end": 87.33,
          "en": "And then NPM start to start the development server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 87.33,
          "end": 88.59,
          "en": "And if you do so,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 88.59,
          "end": 92.013,
          "en": "you should see something like this on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 93.03,
          "end": 96.27000000000001,
          "en": "Some fictional temperature values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 96.27000000000001,
          "end": 100.71000000000001,
          "en": "for various places in the world, a timestamp,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 100.71000000000001,
          "end": 105.663,
          "en": "and then a list of past temperature values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 106.65,
          "end": 109.2,
          "en": "And what you see here on the screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 109.2,
          "end": 112.2,
          "en": "is generated by one single component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 112.2,
          "end": 114.63,
          "en": "It's all in the app component in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 114.63,
          "end": 116.52000000000001,
          "en": "I only got one template here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 116.52000000000001,
          "end": 119.58,
          "en": "because this section is not about components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 119.58,
          "end": 122.61,
          "en": "or directives or anything like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 122.61,
          "end": 124.02,
          "en": "You could, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 124.02,
          "end": 126.72,
          "en": "split this component into multiple components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 126.72,
          "end": 130.47,
          "en": "and you might do that if it were a realistic app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 130.47,
          "end": 133.77,
          "en": "But for this dummy app where we want to focus on pipes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 133.77,
          "end": 136.92000000000002,
          "en": "it's all in one template, all in one component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 136.92000000000002,
          "end": 140.28,
          "en": "And here I got some dummy data in the component class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 140.28,
          "end": 143.223,
          "en": "that is being output in the template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 144.39,
          "end": 148.53,
          "en": "I also got a on reset method here in that class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 148.53,
          "end": 151.05,
          "en": "which is triggered from inside the template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 151.05,
          "end": 154.2,
          "en": "whenever one of these list items here is clicked,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 154.2,
          "end": 158.85,
          "en": "so that it is then changed to 18 as a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 158.85,
          "end": 162.84,
          "en": "So that is the app we'll start with,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 162.84,
          "end": 165.69,
          "en": "and it's in this app where I now want to use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 165.69,
          "end": 167.43,
          "en": "some of the built-in pipes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 167.43,
          "end": 170.25,
          "en": "before we then also build and use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 170.25,
          "end": 173.223,
          "en": "and configure our own custom pipe.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
